WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.400
In this walkthrough we'll create a
new counterparty in the OpenTRMS
Workbench, and make it available for trading.

2
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:11.433
Counterparties live under
Reference data in the left-hand navigation.

3
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:19.800
Start with the legal name. Use the full
registered name exactly as it appears on the
entity's incorporation documents — not a trading alias.

4
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:26.733
Next, choose the counterparty type. The
type drives which credit and margin rules
the risk engine will apply, so it matters.

5
00:00:26.733 --> 00:00:34.067
Set the country of incorporation. This is the
jurisdiction of the legal entity, which is not
always where the desk you deal with is located.

6
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:41.800
Now the Legal Entity Identifier — twenty
alphanumeric characters. The Workbench
validates the check digits before the record can be saved.

7
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.900
Enter the credit limit in US dollars. This is
the gross notional cap across every desk, and
it's enforced at the point of trade capture.

8
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:55.467
Finally, attach a standing settlement
instruction. Without one, trades against
this counterparty will book but will not settle.

9
00:00:55.467 --> 00:01:01.733
Save the counterparty. The record is validated,
written, and an audit entry is raised against your user.

10
00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:08.867
The confirmation gives you the new
counterparty reference. The record is active
immediately and can now be selected during deal entry.
